;; REGRESSION: a `:sequence`-typed slot bound to a fn-ref doesn't
;; surface as a visible edge in the editor's layout.
;;
;; Repro fn-def: `:ex-regression-str-via-ref` — `:str/:parts` is
;; `:sequence`-typed; we bind it to the fn-ref `:_ex-regression-list`
;; (a plain `:list` of literals). At runtime the call works correctly
;; (`:str` joins the three items into "abc"). In the editor, however,
;; navigating to `:ex-regression-str-via-ref` shows ONLY the root card
;; — there is no `parts` edge going to the `:_ex-regression-list`
;; card, even though the binding exists in storage.
;;
;; Same pattern in production: `:web-server`'s router chain ends at
;; `:_router/:routes :all`, and the `:all` fn-card is invisible from
;; web-server unless you navigate to it directly.
;;
;; These fn-defs are exercised by `compile-packages-test/regression-
;; examples-test`, which pins the RUNTIME half (`:str` joins the three
;; items into "abc").
;;
;; The LAYOUT half is pinned by `tools/browser-test/
;; edit-regression-sequence-fn-ref.test.js`, which builds the same shape
;; through the API rather than navigating here: `examples` is dev/test-only
;; and absent from `graphden-executor`, so a browser test pointed at these
;; names could never run in the e2e stack — and for a long time didn't run
;; anywhere at all.


{:namespace "examples.regression.sequence-fn-ref"
 :description "Pins down a layout-pipeline regression: :sequence-typed slot bound to a fn-ref must surface as an edge + downstream fn-card."
 :fns
 [{:name :_ex-regression-list
   :description "A simple list-of-literals. Three string items, joined into \"abc\" when consumed by `:str/:parts` upstream."
   :parent :list
   :args {:items [{:value "a"} {:value "b"} {:value "c"}]}}

  {:name :ex-regression-str-via-ref
   :description "Reproduce the regression: bind the sequence-typed `:parts` slot to a fn-ref. Expected layout: ex-regression-str-via-ref card → `parts` edge → _ex-regression-list card. If the edge or downstream card is missing, the layout BFS dropped the ref."
   :parent :str
   :args {:parts :_ex-regression-list}}]}
